        "original_id": "fc239c75-2f7d-5ca5-834d-387606e86aa5",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Amy Lee, Jimi Hendrix, Dave Eggar, Dave Fortman\n- Organizations: Evanescence\n- Works: War Story, Indigo Grey, Voice from the Stone, Speak to Me, Good Enough\n- Roles: singer, songwriter, record producer, multi-instrumentalist, film score composer, guitarist, producer\n\nFacts:\n- Amy Lee, born Amy Lynn Hartzler née Lee on December 13, 1981, is an American singer, songwriter, record producer, and multi-instrumentalist.\n- Jimi Hendrix's mainstream career lasted only four years, and he is widely regarded as one of the most influential electric guitarists in popular music history and one of the most celebrated musicians of the 20th century.\n- During Evanescence's hiatus, Amy Lee began a film score career in 2013 by composing the soundtrack to War Story, released in 2014, with cellist Dave Eggar.\n- Amy Lee and Dave Eggar also composed the soundtrack to Indigo Grey, released in 2015.\n- Amy Lee wrote the song Speak to Me for the film Voice from the Stone.\n- The Evanescence song Good Enough was written by lead vocalist Amy Lee and produced by Dave Fortman.",
